<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Plot a factored quadratic and state the y-intercept</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A quadratic function is given by \[ y = {@qexpr@}\]</p>
<p><strong>1) Plot it's graph</strong> by dragging the two green points along the \(x\)-axis to the \(x\)-intercepts (roots), and dragging the black point along the \(y\)-axis to the \(y\)-intercept.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans1="rP1" input-ref-ans2="rP2" input-ref-ans3="rP3" width="540px" height="540px"]]
var XLO={#float(xlo)#}, XHI={#float(xhi)#}, YM={#float(ymag)#};
var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[XLO, YM, XHI, -YM], axis:true, grid:true, keepaspectratio:false, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
var P1 = brd.create('glider',[{#sp1#},0,brd.defaultAxes.x],{name:'',color:'#2ca02c',fillColor:'#2ca02c',size:5,snapToGrid:true,snapSizeX:1});
var P2 = brd.create('glider',[{#sp2#},0,brd.defaultAxes.x],{name:'',color:'#2ca02c',fillColor:'#2ca02c',size:5,snapToGrid:true,snapSizeX:1});
var P3 = brd.create('glider',[0,{#sp3y#},brd.defaultAxes.y],{name:'',color:'#000000',fillColor:'#000000',size:5,snapToGrid:true,snapSizeY:1});
function Af(){ var pr=P1.X()*P2.X(); if (Math.abs(pr)<1e-6) return null; return P3.Y()/pr; }
brd.create('functiongraph',[function(x){ var a=Af(); if (a===null) return NaN; return a*(x-P1.X())*(x-P2.X()); }, XLO, XHI],{strokeColor:'#1f4fd8', strokeWidth:2.5, highlight:false});
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP1, P1);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP2, P2);
stack_jxg.bind_point(rP3, P3);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<div style="display:none">[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prtPlot]]</div>
<p><strong>2) State the \(y\)-intercept</strong> of the graph.</p>
<div>\( y = \) [[input:ansYint]] [[validation:ansYint]] [[feedback:prtYint]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>How to plot \(y={@qexpr@}\):</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><p><strong>x-intercepts (roots).</strong></p>
<p> The function is already factorised, so \(y=0\) when \(x={@r1@}\) or \(x={@r2@}\). </p>
<p>Plot \(({@r1@},0)\) and \(({@r2@},0)\).</p></li>
<li><p><strong>y-intercept.</strong></p>
<p> Put \(x=0\): \[ y = {@a@}\,(0-({@r1@}))\,(0-({@r2@})) = {@cc@}. \] </p>
<p>So the curve crosses the \(y\)-axis at \((0,\,{@cc@})\).</p></li>
<li><p><strong>Direction &amp; vertex.</strong></p>
<p> Since \(a={@a@}\), the parabola opens
[[ if test="is(a>0)" ]] upwards [[ else ]] downwards [[/ if ]]; the vertex is halfway between the roots, at \(x={@vx@}\).</p></li>
<li><p><strong>Sketch.</strong></p>
<p> Draw a smooth parabola through the two roots and the y-intercept.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>The \(y\)-intercept is \({@cc@}\) and the graph is shown below.</p>
[[jsxgraph width="500px" height="500px"]]
var A={#a#}, R1={#r1#}, R2={#r2#}, CC={#cc#}, VX={#float(vx)#};
var XLO={#float(xlo)#}, XHI={#float(xhi)#}, YM={#float(ymag)#};
var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[XLO, YM, XHI, -YM], axis:true, grid:true, keepaspectratio:false, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
brd.create('functiongraph',[function(x){ return A*(x-R1)*(x-R2); }, XLO, XHI],{strokeColor:'#1f4fd8', strokeWidth:2.5, highlight:false});
brd.create('point',[R1,0],{name:'',fixed:true,color:'#2ca02c',fillColor:'#2ca02c',size:4});
brd.create('point',[R2,0],{name:'',fixed:true,color:'#2ca02c',fillColor:'#2ca02c',size:4});
brd.create('point',[0,CC],{name:'y-int',fixed:true,color:'#000000',fillColor:'#000000',size:4,label:{offset:[8,-2],cssStyle:'font-weight:bold'}});
brd.create('point',[VX, A*(VX-R1)*(VX-R2)],{name:'',fixed:true,color:'#cc0000',fillColor:'#cc0000',size:3});
[[/jsxgraph]]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
